{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nParent epic `a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb`. This is the behavior-changing story the epic exists for, and\nit lands LAST: it consumes the store from S1 (`248f-ac00-18db-4259`), the snapshot evidence from\nS2 (`83d3-61d9-fc59-424b`), and — critically — the upgrade backfill from S4\n(`f6e9-a5fd-e908-4b82`), without which the first post-upgrade pass would decline every legitimate\nremoval.\n\nThe defect: `managed_refs` is monotonic and marks a ref managed the instant it is created\nLOCALLY, so guard G3 (`inbound_differ.py::_diff_link_removals_inbound`) cannot distinguish a\nnever-pushed local link from a peer-deleted one. G4 (the same-pass outbound-ADD suppression in\n`compute_inbound_mutations`) covers that blind spot ONLY when the outbound differ emits the\nre-ADD — but `outbound_links.py::_diff_links` dedups ADDs direction-agnostically on\n`(vendor_type, target_key)` and is \"intentionally NOT deduped on relation\", so a local link whose\nvendor type collides with an existing remote link in the OTHER direction (local `blocks` against\nan inward `Blocks`, which reads as `depends_on`) is never pushed AND never G4-protected. Its\nremoval record reaches the applier, and since e39f made removal relation-scoped it removes that\nnever-pushed local link.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `peer_confirmations.py` — add `open_store_or_none(repo_root)`, mirroring\n  `apply_inbound_records._open_impossible_link_store`: returns the store, or `None` when it\n  cannot be opened. The helper lives in the new module, NOT in `apply_inbound_records.py`, which\n  has under 50 lines of headroom against the 800-line cap.\n- `apply_inbound_records.py::_inbound_update_apply_links` — open the confirmation store ONCE per\n  pass beside the existing `skip_store = _open_impossible_link_store(repo_root)`, and thread it\n  into `_inbound_unlink_one`. Never re-open per record.\n- `apply_inbound_records.py::_inbound_unlink_one` — gains the store parameter. Before removing,\n  consult `is_confirmed(local_id, target_local_id, relation)`. If NOT confirmed: log a WARNING\n  naming the three key parts and the reason, and `return False` without writing. The return\n  value is load-bearing — `False` keeps the silent-no-op canary in `apply_handlers.py` truthful.\n- **Fail-open:** a `None` store (unopenable) disables the check entirely and restores exactly\n  today's behavior — the record is an optimisation of safety, never a precondition for applying\n  a removal. This mirrors the impossible-link store's stated contract.\n- Existing e39f behavior is preserved unchanged for confirmed links: removal stays\n  relation-scoped via `rebar.unlink(..., relation, ...)`, and a relation with no net-active local\n  link stays a logged INFO no-op.\n- Report the per-pass decline count in the existing `_inbound_update_apply_links` INFO summary\n  that already reports impossible-link skips, so declines are operator-visible rather than\n  log-only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A removal record for a managed link with NO confirmation is declined: no UNLINK event\n      is written, the link is still net-active locally, a WARNING is logged, and\n      `_inbound_unlink_one` returns False. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k declines`.\n- [ ] AC2 A removal record for a link WITH a confirmation still converges — the link is removed,\n      exactly the named relation and no other. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k converges`.\n- [ ] AC3 The epic's motivating scenario end-to-end: a local `blocks` dep whose outbound ADD is\n      deduped by an inward same-vendor-type remote link is NOT removed by an inbound removal\n      record. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k vendor_collision`.\n- [ ] AC4 Re-applying the same declined record on a later pass declines again idempotently and\n      writes nothing. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k idempotent`.\n- [ ] AC5 A backfill-sourced confirmation is sufficient for AC2 (no post-upgrade mass decline).\n      Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k backfill`.\n- [ ] AC6 A `None` (unopenable) store declines nothing — removal behaves exactly as before this\n      story. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k fail_open`.\n- [ ] AC7 The per-pass INFO summary reports the decline count. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k summary`.\n- [ ] AC8 Mutation check: deleting the confirmation check turns the AC1 and AC3 tests RED;\n      restoring it turns them GREEN. Recorded as a ticket comment with both outputs.\n- [ ] AC9 `apply_inbound_records.py` stays under the 800-line cap. Proof: `bash -c 'git archive\n      HEAD | tar -xO src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py | wc -l'` < 800.\n- [ ] AC10 Gates green and no regression. Proof: `make lint` exit 0, `make typecheck` exit 0,\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py` exit 0,\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` exit 0.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New suite `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py`.\n  Tests are BEHAVIORAL, driven through `compute_inbound_mutations` and\n  `_inbound_update_apply_links`, matching the existing 2b16 suite's stated discipline of driving\n  public entry points and never a private helper by name.\n- Regression: the existing `test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py` suite must stay green — its\n  removal-convergence cases now need a confirmation fixture, which is expected and must be added\n  rather than worked around.\n- Full command set: `make lint && make typecheck && pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler`.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nG3 and G4 themselves are unchanged — the discrimination is added at the applier (G5), where the\nepic's acceptance criteria place it. No change to `managed_refs` monotonicity. No change to the\noutbound ADD dedup key."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786560383791153001,"uuid":"40f39ff5-0329-4ee8-91b3-11d07d1a4a41"}